# Crude blending — get the physics right

A plausible-looking wrong answer here teaches false chemistry, which defeats the
point of the app. All 334 streams carry `api`, `sulfur_wt` and `yields`, so no new
data is needed; 211 also have `distillation_curve`.

**API gravity does NOT blend linearly.** Convert to specific gravity, blend by
volume, convert back. Sulfur blends by **mass**, not volume.

```js
const sg  = (api) => 141.5 / (api + 131.5);
const api = (sg)  => 141.5 / sg - 131.5;

// fa = volume fraction of stream a (fb = 1 - fa)
function blend(a, b, fa) {
  const fb = 1 - fa;
  const sgMix = sg(a.api) * fa + sg(b.api) * fb;   // SG: volume-weighted
  const mA = sg(a.api) * fa;                        // mass of each part
  const mB = sg(b.api) * fb;
  const sulfur = (a.sulfur_wt * mA + b.sulfur_wt * mB) / (mA + mB);
  const yields = {};                                // volume-weighted
  for (const k of Object.keys(a.yields)) {
    yields[k] = a.yields[k] * fa + (b.yields[k] || 0) * fb;
  }
  return { api: api(sgMix), sulfur, yields };
}
```

TBP curves blend by volume at each fraction point, same as yields.
On Compare that is a dashed mix line: at each distilled yield, volume-weight
the parents' temperatures. Skip the line if any selected stream has no curve;
do not invent points. 211 of 334 streams have `distillation_curve`.

## Validate, don't assert

Check output against real streams already in `data.js` rather than claiming
accuracy. Arab Light + Basrah Light at 50/50 reproduces Dubai closely:

```
computed:     31.5 API, 2.2% S, yields 19.5 / 28.5 / 26 / 26
dubai actual: 31   API, 2.0% S, yields 18   / 28   / 26 / 28
```

There are 105 `kind: "Blend"` streams and 13 `Dilbit` to test against. Surface a
validation example in the UI so users can see the model is grounded.

## Honest limits

Blending is near-linear for gravity, sulfur and bulk yields, but **not** for
viscosity, pour point, or asphaltene stability — incompatible crudes can flocculate
asphaltenes. Say so rather than implying a blend is always physically fine.
